mcp|stdio|server|client|notifications/roots/list_changed = waived 2026-08-12 busbar is not itself launched as a child process. The stdio SERVER direction means an agent spawns `busbar` and speaks MCP on its stdin -- one gateway process per client, with no listener, no TLS, no admin plane and no shared store. Every control busbar exists to apply is scoped to a long-lived multi-tenant listener: virtual keys, budgets, the audience validation that is the confused-deputy defence, the per-call log chain, the trust lifecycle. None of them means anything inside one client's own child process, and a busbar that served MCP there would be a governance gateway with the governance switched off. The OUTBOUND stdio direction is implemented instead, which is the one a gateway is for: busbar fronts local stdio MCP servers on behalf of many callers. Reversible -- it is a product decision, not a technical block.
